    "body": "I had a new idea. Why don't we say that platform objects may define themselves as \"not serializable for storage\", in addition to their serialization/deserialization steps? And explain when you might want to do that. Then we just throw a DataCloneError if that is set for a platform object.\r\n\r\nThat would help enforce consistent errors, for example.",
